      "result": "## Job Board Application Test Summary\n\nI have completed the comprehensive testing of the job board web application against all 19 checklist items. Here are the results:\n\n### ✅ **PASSED: 14 Items**\nThe application successfully implements:\n- **Core Functionality**: Job posting, deletion (with confirmation), browsing, and application submission\n- **Job Seeker Features**: Complete job search, filtering by industry/location/type, keyword search, and detailed job views\n- **Employer Dashboard**: Accurate job and application counting, application list viewing with full details\n- **Data Persistence**: Published jobs and applications persist after page reload\n- **Content Display**: All job cards and detail pages show complete information (title, company, industry, type, location, salary, posting date, skills)\n- **Application Tracking**: Submission dates and applicant details (name, email, phone, message) are properly displayed\n\n### ❌ **FAILED: 5 Items**\n\n**1. FT-18: Job Edit Functionality**\n- Edit feature is not implemented\n- No edit button in dashboard or accessible edit URL\n\n**2. CS-9: Application Form Validation**\n- Missing required field validation with no error messages\n- Invalid email addresses are not rejected with feedback\n- Users can submit incomplete forms without error notification\n\n**3. CS-10: Job Publishing Validation**\n- No validation feedback for missing required fields\n- Invalid salary ranges (min > max) are not flagged with error messages\n- Form submission is silently prevented without user guidance\n\n**4. CS-11: Duplicate Email Prevention**\n- Duplicate applications using the same email overwrite existing applications rather than being rejected\n- Users receive a success message when the application actually violates the constraint\n- No clear feedback about why the duplicate cannot be accepted\n\n**5. Validation/Error Messaging Gap**\n- The application lacks comprehensive form validation with clear, user-friendly error messages\n- This impacts both job seekers and employers during data entry\n\n### 📊 **Overall Assessment**\nThe job board application has solid core functionality with **73.7% compliance** (14/19 items passing). The main improvements needed are implementing form validation with clear error messaging and the job editing feature.",
